    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a challenging slate today, but the optimizer favors our heavy hitters against vulnerable arms. **Kyle Tucker** (75.29) and **Andy Pages** (70.97) anchor the lineup against Pfaadt; both benefit significantly from the matchup's SP_xERA of 4.54, with **Andy Pages** gaining a specific efficiency boost from Pfaadt\u2019s slow delivery, which keeps our stolen base potential high. **Jacob Wilson** (66.47) and **Jackson Merrill** (64.78) also present as strong starts. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces the elite velocity of deGrom, his 60.75 score holds steady due to his consistent plate appearances at the top of the order and a favorable platoon profile that helps mitigate the threat of a top-tier arm.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Heliot Ramos**, who narrowly missed the cut at 46.60. While he offers solid raw output, the presence of Sale (2.92 xERA) on the mound created too much risk compared to the higher-floor matchups of **Luis Robert Jr.** (59.58) and **Jorge Polanco** (55.88). Although **Luis Robert Jr.** faces a lower-tier starter in Chandler, we are monitoring the catcher pop time (1.89s), which slightly suppresses his stolen base upside; nevertheless, his ability to exploit Chandler\u2019s slow delivery keeps him firmly in the UTIL spot. We are also tracking **Sam Antonacci** (46.73); while his score is lower, his status as a leadoff hitter remains valuable. Please note that **Jordan Westburg** remains on the IL, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is not in the active lineup today, so we are proceeding without their production.",
